---
/**
 * Systems → Influence & Reputation (Figma node 975:494).
 * Dark variant, now the shipped page — the light version (Figma node
 * 927:1254) has been retired. Kept its three additions over the plain
 * light layout (see the three inline comments below marking them: the
 * Addons CTA + auto-rotating carousel, the Selected Projects arrows, and
 * the dark→light reveal on Impact + Selected Projects).
 *
 * COLOR STRATEGY: everything from Hero through Addons is wrapped in
 * `.dark-zone`, a single scoped rule that redefines the site's semantic
 * --color-surface/ink/ink-secondary/line tokens to their dark equivalents.
 * Custom properties inherit through the DOM regardless of Astro's style
 * scoping (scoping only limits which elements the *selector* matches, not
 * how the properties it sets cascade), so every shared component below —
 * Heading, SectionIntro, ProjectCard, SystemProblemCards, PhasesScroll,
 * SystemExpertiseRotator — renders dark automatically through the same
 * `text-ink`/`bg-surface`/`bg-line` classes those components always use,
 * with no per-component dark prop needed. (SystemExpertiseRotator and the
 * two pinned sections' progress bars were the only hardcoded-not-token
 * colors among them; fixed at the component level, see git history.)
 *
 * Impact, Selected Projects, the Contact CTA and the Footer are NOT in
 * `.dark-zone` — the Figma frame keeps those white even in the dark
 * variant, EXCEPT Impact reads dark on first arrival (matching the Addons
 * section above it) and only turns light once scrolled further. Impact +
 * Selected Projects share one `.reveal-zone` (see that section below) —
 * ONE background-color covering both, so they can never be caught
 * mid-scroll with one dark and one light — which starts dark and flips to
 * the same light palette the CTA/Footer already use the instant the
 * zone's (=Impact's) own top edge reaches the top of the viewport. Same
 * mechanism (a boolean `--light-progress` custom property, ScrollTrigger
 * `start: 'top top'`, onEnter/onLeaveBack, fast CSS transition) as the
 * homepage's own light→dark invert-zone (src/pages/index.astro), just
 * running the other direction.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { navItems } from '../../../lib/nav'
import Heading from '../../../components/Heading.astro'
import SectionIntro from '../../../components/SectionIntro.astro'
